<title>USA: News sees $800 mln in 96 cash flow.</title>
<headline>News sees $800 mln in 96 cash flow.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>News Corp Ltd Vice-President of Finance and Banking William Sorenson said on Friday that he expects the Australia-based media conglomerate to post US$800 million cash flow in calendar 1996, after interest capital expenditures and taxes.</p>
<p>Sorenson, in remarks at the PaineWebber media conference here, said the comparable number in 1995 was &quot;north of US$500 million&quot; but declined to provide additional detail.</p>
<p>He also said News Corp has US$3.1 billion of cash, and about US$1 billion after refinancing and other commitments, including the acquisition of New World Communications Group Inc, announced in September.</p>
<p>Sorenson said currently, News Corp is &quot;not looking to buy anybody big.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brendan Intindola, Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1734</p>
